data: {"type": "final", "payload": "## 核查结论\n\n**该论断获得\"部分支持\"——RAG 确实被广泛认为能降低幻觉风险,但证据多为\"有前景/缓解\"的定性表述,且文献同时指出其引入的新问题,因此不能视为无条件的充分成立。**\n\n**支持证据(占主导)**\n多篇文献明确将 RAG 定位为缓解 LLM 幻觉的可行手段:\n- 《Retrieval-Augmented Generation and Hallucination in Large Language Models: A Scholarly Overview》(2025)称 RAG 是\"通过将模型输出锚定在检索证据上来缓解幻觉的有前景技术\";\n- 《MS-RAG: Simple and Effective Multi-Semantic Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2025)与《Benchmarking Large Language Models in Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2023)均把 RAG 描述为\"缓解幻觉的广泛采用/有前景方法\";\n- 《ReRag: A New Architecture for Reducing the Hallucination by Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2024)直接以\"降低幻觉\"为架构目标。\n\n**审慎限定(证据的边界)**\n核查结果中支持证据 6 条、反驳 0 条,但支持句多为\"promising/mitigate/alleviate\"这类方向性表述,而非严格的因果或量化结论。同时,领域综述《Hallucination Mitigation for Retrieval-Augmented Large Language Models: A Review》(2025)和《Removal of Hallucination on Hallucination: Debate-Augmented RAG》(2025)等指出:RAG 本身会引入**检索错误、检索偏差(检索谄媚)或错误证据**等新问题,若检索质量不佳,反而可能放大幻觉。因此 RAG 降低幻觉是有条件的——依赖检索质量与证据相关性。\n\n**结论**\nRAG 降低幻觉风险这一论断在文献库中有较强方向性支持,但属于\"部分支持\":它作为缓解幻觉的主流技术路径成立,却并非无条件保证,其效果受检索质量制约,且可能引入新的幻觉来源。若需更严格的因果结论,现有证据(多为定性表述)尚不足以支撑\"必然/显著降低\"的强断言。", "meta": {"runtime": "langgraph", "node": "reflect", "phase": "自检修正", "elapsed_ms": 845, "session_id": "t04-20260812T134352Z-run-3", "stop_reason": "completed", "tokens_in": 5891, "tokens_out": 439, "structured_answer": {"schema_version": "answer-contract/v1", "capability": "claim_verification", "status": "partially_supported", "verdict_label": "部分支持", "answer_mode": "evidence_based", "citation_compliance": "ok", "citations": [{"paper_id": "W4411065983", "title": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation and Hallucination in Large Language Models: A Scholarly Overview", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "85598e54abed9ffbc0fdb9a455d979f064cc365d", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has emerged as a promising technique to mitigate hallucinations by grounding mo", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.8}, {"paper_id": "W4416035754", "title": "MS-RAG: Simple and Effective Multi-Semantic Retrieval-Augmented Generation", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "7a23375ff75a4c1cfa1b95bb4ed4218bc9134c1b", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "To alleviate the hallucination problem of large language model (LLM), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) has been proposed and widely adopted.", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.8}, {"paper_id": "W4405272436", "title": "ReRag: A New Architecture for Reducing the Hallucination by Retrieval- Augmented Generation", "year": 2024, "chunk_uid": "d5ab39c21c6253bb31d68dc0d60ab2b9d753c40d", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Recently, Retrieval-Augmented Generation systems (RAG) have been introduced to cope with this problem.", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.7}, {"paper_id": "2309.01431", "title": "Benchmarking Large Language Models in Retrieval-Augmented Generation", "year": 2023, "chunk_uid": "a36067aaf8a0b7b5f7075ba84805001d3ef35f51", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a promising approach for mitigating the hallucination of large language models (LLMs).", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.8}], "uncertainty": {"category": "none", "message": "", "calibrated_rejection": false, "qualification_hints": []}, "tool_basis": ["verify_claim"], "claim": "检索增强生成（RAG）能够降低大语言模型回答中的幻觉风险"}}}

